Concise:

The frontend uses Vue 3, with Apexcharts for data visualization (charts) and Mapbox for maps. The backend is powered by Go.
Slightly more descriptive:

For the frontend, we're leveraging Vue 3. Data visualization is handled by Apexcharts for charts and Mapbox for interactive maps. The backend is built with Go.
More formal/technical:

The frontend implementation utilizes Vue 3. Apexcharts is employed for charting and data visualization, while Mapbox is used for geographical mapping. The backend is developed using the Go language.

The components are the dashboard's visual elements. They include statistical data (charts), spatial data (maps), and some historical data.

For data formatting, please refer to the following frontend technical documentation:

"Chart Data" (for chart data styles): https://tuic.gov.taipei/documentation/front-end/chart-data
"Map Data" (for spatial data styles): https://tuic.gov.taipei/documentation/front-end/map-data
And for the backend:

"Component Data APIs" (for component data APIs): https://tuic.gov.taipei/documentation/back-end/component-data-apis